This distribution changes user-facing branding from Continue to NextCLI and
turns off calls to Continue-hosted services:

- Docs, extension display names, and the CLI banner say NextCLI.
- Repository links for this project point at https://github.com/nextcli-dev/nextcli.
- There is no default hosted API. api.continue.dev, hub sign-in, and the
  model proxy are not used unless CONTINUE_API_BASE or an explicit base URL
  is set.
- Anonymous telemetry is off unless it is explicitly enabled, and it is not
  sent to Continue. Sentry is not initialized unless NEXTCLI_SENTRY_DSN is
  provided. This tree no longer contains a hard-coded Continue Sentry DSN.

The following identifiers are unchanged so existing installs keep working:
@continuedev/* package names, the VS Code publisher and extension id, the
`cn` command, and the ~/.continue config directory. NextCLI does not ship a
JetBrains plugin. In a JetBrains IDE, run `cn` in the terminal.